    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1050">

                <pb facs="1343" n="1333" xml:id="pg1333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.52/10–1846</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-11-29T19:00:00-05:00">November 29,
                            1946—7 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2173. Dept perceives no objection to application by American interests for
                    registration and issuance new title deeds accordance procedure outlined Urtel
                    2034 Oct 18. Interested Americans should be informed however that such
                    documentation prepared in ConGen only prima facie evidence American ownership as
                    question one for judicial decision Chinese authorities. As indicated Deptel 2048
                    Nov 8<anchor n="38" xml:id="d1050-f1"/> notarial services this connection may be
                    performed gratis under Item 38. Care should be exercised in ascertaining
                    American interests are protected fullest extent contemplated Article 4, 1943
                    treaty (Sent Shanghai, repeated Nanking as Dept’s 1104).</p>
                <p>ConGen authorized apply for new deed ownership Whangpoo Road property (Urtels
                    2044 Oct 21 and 2247 Nov 15<anchor n="39" xml:id="d1050-f2"/>) including
                    submerged areas subject reclamation. Copies new deeds govt property should be
                    forwarded Dept.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1050-f1" n="38" xml:id="d1050-f1-content">
